1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:07,689
In 1884 he arrived in New York to work for the most famous inventor in the world: Thomas Edison.

2
00:00:07,909 --> 00:00:19,370
Edison lit the city with direct current, and his entire business depended on it. According to Tesla, he was promised fifty thousand dollars if he improved their generators.

3
00:00:19,570 --> 00:00:27,109
He worked for months barely sleeping. When he went to collect, they told him it had been a joke. He quit.

4
00:00:27,309 --> 00:00:36,078
Tesla started his own company and his partners pushed him out. He ended up digging ditches in the street for two dollars a day.

5
00:00:36,278 --> 00:00:41,201
The foreman heard him talking about his motor and introduced him to a group of investors.

6
00:00:41,401 --> 00:00:46,940
He told them about the Egg of Columbus, who according to legend stood an egg upright by tapping its tip.

7
00:00:47,140 --> 00:00:54,216
Tesla placed a copper egg on the table, switched on his current… and the egg spun until it stood upright.

8
00:00:54,416 --> 00:01:01,186
It was his invisible magnet, spinning beneath the wood. They put up the money. Remember that egg.

9
00:01:02,086 --> 00:01:06,624
Columbus had to crack the egg. Tesla made it dance.
